# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file specifies code ownership patterns and team review requirements.
# GitHub uses CODEOWNERS to automatically request reviews from designated teams.
#
# IMPORTANT: Pattern Matching Order
# GitHub matches the LAST matching pattern for each file, so order matters.
# More specific rules should generally come after general ones to ensure specificity wins.
#
# PLACEHOLDER TEAMS
# The team handles below (@team-backend, @team-web, @team-mobile, @team-devops)
# are GENERIC PLACEHOLDERS and MUST be replaced with real GitHub team handles
# before this file is activated or enforced.
#
# Expected format: @org-name/team-slug
# Example: @mycompany/backend-team, @mycompany/platform-team
#
# Until real team handles are configured, CODEOWNERS entries with no matching teams
# simply have no effect — GitHub will not request reviews, but it won't break anything.
#
# Uncomment and update the lines below with real GitHub team handles to enable enforcement.

# Backend application
# /apps/api/ @team-backend

# Web application
# /apps/web/ @team-web

# Mobile application
# /apps/mobile/ @team-mobile

# Infrastructure and DevOps
# /infra/ @team-devops

# Shared packages
# /packages/shared/ @team-devops

# GitHub workflows and configuration
# /.github/ @team-devops
